.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_config" "fuzzygene_config"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_config \- Create a FuzzyGene modelling configuration object.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_config(\fBmaxRegulators\fR as integer = 4, 
\fBselection\fR as string = "prior-first", 
\fBminCorrelation\fR as double = 0.3, 
\fBmode\fR as string = "auto", 
\fBmfCount\fR as integer = 3, 
\fBmfKind\fR as string = "gaussian", 
\fBmaxEpoch\fR as integer = 100, 
\fBlearningRate\fR as double = 0.02, 
\fBpruneThreshold\fR as double = 0.01, 
\fBmaxGenes\fR as integer = 2000, 
\fBmaxTrainRows\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBmaxCandidateGenes\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBminBestCorrelation\fR as double = 0, 
\fBnoveltyQuota\fR as double = 0, 
\fBrulePartition\fR as string = "auto", 
\fBscatterRules\fR as integer = 48, 
\fBscatterInputs\fR as integer = 8, 
\fBscatterMinInputs\fR as integer = 2, 
\fBscatterZThreshold\fR as double = 1, 
\fBscatterSeed\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBmaxRules\fR as integer = 128, 
\fBmaxConsequentParams\fR as integer = 512, 
\fBstandardize\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBpropagationSteps\fR as integer = 50, 
\fBrelaxation\fR as double = 0.5, 
\fBknockdownResidual\fR as double = 0.2, 
\fBoverexpressionSigmas\fR as double = 3, 
\fBsignificanceZScore\fR as double = 2, 
\fBdegreeOfParallelism\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBminTimePoints\fR as integer = 3, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Create a FuzzyGene modelling configuration object.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBmaxRegulators\fB \fR\- 
 how many candidate regulators (ANFIS inputs) are kept per target gene. The rule count of a
 grid partition is `m^n`, so this is the primary guard against the rule explosion;
 3-6 is the practically useful range. Default 4.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBselection\fB \fR\- 
 regulator selection strategy: \fBprior-first\fR (default, prior edges by confidence then
 correlation), \fBcorrelation\fR (data driven only) or \fBprior\fR (prior edges only).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBminCorrelation\fB \fR\- 
 minimum |Pearson| for a gene to be taken as a correlation based regulator. Default 0.3.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmode\fB \fR\- 
 fit route: \fBauto\fR (default, lagged when the matrix has at least \fBminTimePoints\fR distinct
 time points), \fBstatic\fR or \fBlagged\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmfCount\fB \fR\- number of membership functions per input. Default 3.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmfKind\fB \fR\- 
 membership function shape: \fBgaussian\fR, \fBbell\fR, \fBsigmoid\fR, \fBtriangular\fR or
 \fBtrapezoidal\fR. Default \fBgaussian\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmaxEpoch\fB \fR\- maximum training epochs per target gene. Default 100.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlearningRate\fB \fR\- learning rate of the premise parameter optimizer. Default 0.02.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpruneThreshold\fB \fR\- 
 rules whose average normalized firing strength falls below this value are pruned after
 training; 0 disables pruning. Default 0.01.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmaxGenes\fB \fR\- 
 upper bound on the number of modelled genes (highest variance first, prior TFs always kept);
 0 keeps everything. Default 2000.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmaxTrainRows\fB \fR\- 
 maximum number of training rows per target gene; 0 uses every row. The dominant cost of the
 hybrid learning is the least squares normal equations, which scale as
 `rows x P^2`, so capping the rows is the cheapest large speedup: a few thousand rows
 are already far more than the few hundred consequent parameters need.
 Default 0 (all rows); 3000-5000 is the recommended setting for genome scale data.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmaxCandidateGenes\fB \fR\- 
 size limit of the candidate pool used by the correlation screening
 (prior TFs plus the highest variance genes); 0 screens every gene. The screening cost is
 `O(genes^2 x rows)`, which at genome scale becomes comparable with the training itself.
 Default 0; 2000-4000 is the recommended setting for genome scale data.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBminBestCorrelation\fB \fR\- 
 skip a target gene when it has no prior regulator and its best |Pearson| against the
 candidates is below this value (such models have R2 close to 0). 0 disables the filter.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBnoveltyQuota\fB \fR\- 
 fraction (0-1) of the regulator slots reserved for genes that are **not** in the prior
 network of that target, i.e. for links discovered from the expression data.
 \fB0\fR (default) keeps the old "prior first" behaviour, where prior TFs can occupy every
 slot and the model can only repeat the prior. \fB0.2\fR-\fB0.4\fR is a sensible range:
 with K = 6 and \fB0.34\fR two slots are always given to data driven regulators.
 Ignored when \fBselection = "prior-only"\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBrulePartition\fB \fR\- 
 rule generation strategy: \fBauto\fR (default), \fBgrid\fR or \fBscatter\fR.
 \fBgrid\fR places m membership functions per input and enumerates `m^K` rules, so the rule
 count explodes with the input count. \fBscatter\fR clusters the training samples (kmeans) and
 creates one rule per cluster, each with its own gaussian center/width per input - the number of
 rules no longer depends on K, which is what makes \fBmaxRegulators = 18\fR feasible.
 \fBauto\fR keeps \fBgrid\fR while `m^K <= maxRules` and `m^K*(K+1) <= maxConsequentParams`,
 otherwise it switches to \fBscatter\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBscatterRules\fB \fR\- number of clusters (= rules) of the scatter partition. Default 48.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBscatterInputs\fB \fR\- maximum number of antecedents per scatter rule. Default 8.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBscatterMinInputs\fB \fR\- minimum number of antecedents per scatter rule. Default 2.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBscatterZThreshold\fB \fR\- 
 an input joins a cluster rule when the cluster center deviates from the global mean by at
 least this many standard deviations. Default 1.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBscatterSeed\fB \fR\- random seed of the clustering, keeps the structure reproducible. Default 0.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmaxRules\fB \fR\- rule budget per target gene. Default 128.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmaxConsequentParams\fB \fR\- consequent parameter budget per target gene. Default 512.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBstandardize\fB \fR\- z-score the expression matrix before fitting. Default TRUE.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpropagationSteps\fB \fR\- maximum fixed point iterations of a perturbation. Default 50.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBrelaxation\fB \fR\- damping factor of the fixed point iteration. Default 0.5.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBknockdownResidual\fB \fR\- 
 fraction of the baseline expression retained after a virtual knockdown. Default 0.2.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBoverexpressionSigmas\fB \fR\- 
 overexpression level in training standard deviations above the baseline. Default 3.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsignificanceZScore\fB \fR\- |z| threshold used to flag a gene as significantly changed. Default 2.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdegreeOfParallelism\fB \fR\- per-gene training parallelism; 0 = all cores, 1 = serial.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBminTimePoints\fB \fR\- distinct time points required to switch to the lagged route. Default 3.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment (unused, kept for error reporting symmetry). 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a validated configuration object
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The returned object (registered as the \fBfuzzygene_config\fR R# type) is accepted by the
 \fBconfig\fR argument of \fBfuzzygene::build_fuzzygene\fR. Structure and training options are
 inherited from the shared ANFIS configuration; this api exposes the subset that matters for
 gene regulatory network inference.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
